ot digests:\n\n- Initial/reload: `97fc180d4d35c68ca5941dc591afb315220550165469f3c4ead7827989cc2f3f`.\n- 960x600: `c4b5bcb99dc3128579c0847289be0f164bed9bac4f835a58c34d488ee728d5c7`.\n- 600x900: `406cda33e04527d15c940507c117c9330a5e04c314deb0ce8a27c6e4559f421a`.\n- 1920x1080: `4eb985843ec4c3da315e37e806eb3586bf59ce291c45f5b0f680025bda5d650a`.\n\nProduction HTML, loader, main, viewport and WASM match the frozen build; the\npublished manifest's expected URL rewrite has SHA-256\n`f9167b5f37964ffc614e3c5dc4bce99f2bf8a804a226fb02181c6a42761203e0`.\nThe active SW's executed VERSION/CACHE is checked in its own worker context,\nnot inferred only from a network fetch. The corrected per-phase/active-build\nchecks include missing-reload-artifact and stale-controller sabotage fixtures.\n\nClaim: black-screen recovery and host-side fitting are implemented and shipped,\nwith reproducible recorded production GUI evidence. The public run took about\n173 seconds to first desktop readiness and 149 seconds after reload. This is\nnot a fast-boot, responsive-input, guest-modeset, full Omarchy or Epic 6 claim.\nThe prior broad `make ci` platform failures remain disclosed above; the fresh\nverifier decides only the scoped rendering task's status.\n\n### 2026-09-10 — verifier — VERDICT: verified\n\n- **Artifact/pair integrity — HELD.** Frozen R3 kernel, immutable base manifest,\n  RAM and delta identities match the immediate, exact-head cold-clone and\n  deployed production reports. Raw-manifest, mixed-pair and missing/corrupt\n  artifact attacks fail closed without a mutable fallback or durable guest\n  state.\n- **Immediate restored repaint — HELD.** `immediate/report.json` binds current\n  WASM `c48e9c2d...b9305` and the exact R3 pair; display callback count advances\n  0→1 with `guestRunCalls=0`, 413 sampled colors and 96.1489% visible pixels.\n  The verifier carried the directly inspected real bar/Foot screenshot.\n- **Built page, reload and fitting — HELD.** The exact-head scrubbed col